From: EglantinePS5
Subject: [PATCH] up: EDEN_UP_GPU_READ_THROUGH hook: the GPU side's reads of guest memory (DeviceMemoryManager ReadBlock/ReadBlockUnsafe, MemoryManager ReadBlockImpl/ReadBlockUnsafe, GuestMemory read spans) go through a copy the front may set; GPU threads name themselves to the front; inert unless the front sets it

The front's guest memory service (src/guest_memory_service.inc, EDEN_UP_GPU_READ_THROUGH=1) sets
Common::GuestReadThrough::copy_fn and readable_fn through eden_core_set_guest_read_through. Then a
read of a guest slot that is packed (EDEN_GUEST_SWAP=3) or in the swap file is copied from its packed
bytes into the read's destination, under the slot's lock, without a block for the slot: the GPU back
thread no longer faults there and waits in the fault handler for a block that only it could free
(T166 drain A/B, runs 1399 and 1402: SIGSEGV in memcpy under ReadBlockImpl <- GuestMemory::Read <-
UploadImageContents, and under WalkBlock <- ReadBlockUnsafe <- AheadGuard::Read <- ReadGuestForBuffer).
A read-only GuestMemory whose direct span would cover such a slot takes the copy path instead.

BackLoop (GPUBack) and the GPU thread call the front's weak eden_guest_gpu_thread_mark(1|2), so its
fault handler can tell them apart (EDEN_UP_FAULT_RESERVE, EDEN_UP_FAULT_LOG).

Unset: copy_fn and readable_fn stay null; each read is the same memcpy after one relaxed load of a
null pointer, and spans are handed out as before. Files: common/guest_read_through.h (new),
core/device_memory_manager.inc, core/guest_memory.h, video_core/memory_manager.cpp,
video_core/gpu_split.cpp, video_core/gpu_thread.cpp. None is a translation id input (not in
SINGLE, not reached from src/shader_recompiler), no name in TranslationSwitches: KEEPS THE STORE.
